'''zumbooruk''' (zum′bọ-ruk), ''n.'' [Also ''zumbooruck'', ''zomboruk'', ''zamboorak''; < Hind. Pers. Ar. ''zambūrak'', < Turk. ''zambūrak'', a small gun, dim. of Ar. ''zambūr'', a hornet.] A small cannon mounted on a swivel, usually shorter and with larger bore than the zingal. {{smaller|In English writings the name is especially applied to such a piece carried on a camel, the pivot which supports it being erected on the saddle in front of the rider.}}
